{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":104354,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aaf7ccf8-74e9-4844-b9be-e5eba03a02a8","total_cost_usd":0.874544,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62518,"cache_read_input_tokens":20654,"output_tokens":7688,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":62518,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7688,"cache_read_input_tokens":20654,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":62518},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":46742,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.046827,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7688,"cacheReadInputTokens":20654,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62518,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.827717,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this config is a bottom-band-only game: the base ship reaches only the 65 km sample and arrives with 1.4% of tank, the hold weighs 121.5 kg instead of the ~743 kg the params assume, and Armstrong's module survives no descent at any skim count from any sample altitude.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"module_finale_infeasible_at_every_altitude\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"Armstrong's module plunges at 268.8 bar units and comes home on one braking pass at 196.5, under the 208 base heat capacity, so the finale is an aerobraking flight that every shield tier can fly.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Committed descents with the 8,000 m floor give the module a plunge peak of 245.3 (bottom), 294.6 (middle) and 368.3 (top), and a best skimmed peak of 223.3 / 231.5 / 231.3 — survives:false in all twelve cells. The best case anywhere, 223.3 from the bottom sample, is 7.4% over the 208 base capacity and only 6.2% under the 238 maxed tier; from the top of the band, where the module actually hangs, the best skimmed peak is 231.3 against a 238 ceiling — 2.8% of margin. The params' 196.5 skimmed figure is not reproduced anywhere in the sweep.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"base_ship_cannot_leave_the_bottom_sample\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"The base ship reaches the floor of the band on a ballistic arc with 29.5% of its tank left and a 97-second EVA window, and the first tank tier turns the hop into a stay.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Bottom sample: arc reached, apex 72,880 m, EVA window 118.9 s, but fuel_remaining_kg 5.72 — a 1.4% margin, not 29.5%, and orbit_reached false ('out of fuel before circularising'). Middle and top: reached false, 'crashed on ascent', apex 84,977 m and 89,362 m against targets of 115,000 m and 215,000 m. The climb itself is safe — peak 53.3 bar units, 26% of the 208 capacity, close to the GDD's 47.5 — so this is delta-v, not heat.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_is_a_fifth_of_the_mass_it_is_priced_at\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.4\",\n      \"claim\": \"Seven slots at the catalog's mean is 742.7 kg of cargo, so a full hold lands at 1,392.7 kg — 2.14x dry mass, 'roughly doubling' the ship, and reproducing the GDD's flown ~1,398 kg.\",\n      \"measured\": \"kg_per_slot 17.36, full_hold_kg 121.5, full_hold_mass_ratio 1.19. The flown full-hold mass is 771.5 kg, not 1,392.7. Every downstream number the balancer derived from the heavier hold moves with it: staged ballistic coefficient is 132.7 kg/m2 empty (fine, well above the 50 floor) but the loaded case never reaches the 285 kg/m2 the Researcher priced.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"greed_costs_nothing_measurable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.4\",\n      \"claim\": \"Every stowed piece is permanent mass for the ride down; the hold-mass scale's green/amber/red zones mark where a competent deploy lands soft, hard or destructive.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Across all three samples, empty vs full hold moves touchdown speed from 3.00 to 3.27 m/s and single-pass peak heat from 65-71 to 71-77 — both loads land soft with the same pass count and the same plate cost (11.8% vs 12.5% at the top). The scale has no amber or red to point at below the module. The grid agrees this is hard to buy: greed_costs_something is satisfied by 16.7% of 5,184 configurations.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"one_pass_is_cheapest_everywhere_confirmed\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.optimal_skims is 0 at all three samples and the cost curve minimises at k=0; the design takes its multi-pass requirement from heat capacity, not from cost.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Confirmed, without exception: cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all twelve descent cells, and the toll grows as stated — top-band empty runs 11.8% of plate at one pass, 95.9% at four, 15,396% at thirteen. The grid backs the mechanism rather than the cost rule: skimming_cools_the_entry holds in 88.3% of worlds and skim_benefit_saturates in 88.9%, so the withdrawal of the '2-4 passes should be cheapest' goal in GDD §5 is correct and should stay withdrawn.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skim_multipliers_understate_the_measured_ratio\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier is [1, 0.48, 0.45, 0.44] and one skim is worth 0.42-0.53x on the peak.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Measured multipliers are band-dependent and only match at the top: bottom [1, 0.702, 0.702, 0.702], middle [1, 0.524, 0.524, 0.524], top [1, 0.439, 0.439, 0.439]. The stated single-vector value is 46% optimistic at the bottom sample. Saturation after the first skim is exact — the second and third skims move the peak by zero at every sample and every entry depth scanned.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parachute_claim_contradicted_but_for_the_right_reason\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3\",\n      \"claim\": \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms 4.4 at 480 m2 and Cd 1.8, 12% under the 5.0 m/s soft line.\",\n      \"measured\": \"measured_full_hold_ms 3.27 against a claimed 4.4 — delta 1.13 m/s, and independent:true, so the canopy is stated and the speed is flown rather than solved backwards. The disagreement is entirely the hold mass: the flight massed 771.5 kg where the params assumed 1,392.7 kg, and sqrt(771.5/1392.7) x 4.4 = 3.28. Fix the hold mass and this claim comes back; until then the parachute purchase has no work to do.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_braking_pass_is_not_survivable_low\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"Braking passes may be flown staged or unstaged, and it is a real choice: 3x heat buys the ability to steer between passes.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Unstaged shallow pass peaks at 424 bar units from the bottom sample (survivable:false against a 208-238 ladder) and 88 from the middle (survivable:true) — the choice exists in one of the two sampled bands and is a certain kill in the other. Across the grid, unstaged_pass_survivable is the rarest target in the whole space: 8.0% of 5,184 configurations, and not one of the thirteen top-scoring worlds satisfies it. No tuning of this config reaches it; if the unstaged option matters, the 3x multiplier is the thing to move, not the capacity ladder.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"difficulty_rises_with_altitude_only_when_the_floor_binds\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"Value and risk rise together with altitude, so the gradient alone produces the difficulty curve.\",\n      \"measured\": \"With entry depth free, difficulty falls with altitude: empty-ship single-pass peak heat is 71 at the bottom sample, 67 at the middle, 65 at the top, and plate cost falls 12.5% to 11.8%. With the 8,000 m commit floor applied it reverses — empty plunge 94.1 / 116.7 / 148.9, module plunge 245.3 / 294.6 / 368.3. The curve is a product of the commit floor, not of the band. The grid rate is 55.9%, so it is reachable, but it is the floor doing the work and cutting the floor would inverse the curve.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"cargo.base_slots\",\n      \"current\": 7,\n      \"proposed\": 13,\n      \"reason\": \"At the flown 17.36 kg per slot, 13 slots is 225.7 kg and a 1.35x mass ratio — still short of the doubling, but it is the only lever inside these files; the real fix is a heavier low-band catalog, which is the Debris Designer's to move, and until it does the parachute and heat-shield tracks have almost nothing to counterweight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 420,\n      \"proposed\": 560,\n      \"reason\": \"A 1.4% margin at the bottom sample is a coin-flip first launch, not the GDD's 29.5%; +140 kg is the tier-1 tank value already in the shop and buys the arc real margin, at the cost of a heavier liftoff and one less obvious job for the tank upgrade.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms\",\n      \"current\": 4.4,\n      \"proposed\": 3.27,\n      \"reason\": \"Restates the claim as the number the canopy actually produced at the flown hold mass; costs the parachute upgrade its stated justification until the hold mass is fixed, which is the honest position.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.48, 0.45, 0.44],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.702, 0.702, 0.702],\n      \"reason\": \"Uses the measured bottom-sample vector — the worst case and the one the first braking pass a player flies will produce — so the plate budget stops assuming a discount the low band does not give; every ablation cost derived from it rises.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index.top\",\n      \"current\": 144.7,\n      \"proposed\": 148.9,\n      \"reason\": \"The measured empty-ship plunge peak from the top sample with the commit floor in place; a 2.9% correction that keeps the index honest against the flight rather than against the balancer's arithmetic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades.5.value\",\n      \"current\": 222,\n      \"proposed\": 232,\n      \"reason\": \"Heat-shield tier 1 raised so the module's measured best skimmed peak of 223.3 from the bottom sample clears at mid-tier; still far below the 368.3 top-band plunge, so no tier buys the plunge back.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades.11.value\",\n      \"current\": 238,\n      \"proposed\": 252,\n      \"reason\": \"Heat-shield tier 2 raised so the module's measured 231.3 top-band skimmed peak clears by 9% instead of 2.8%, making the finale flyable at full upgrades; it stays 31% below the 368.3 plunge peak, so the endgame's mechanic survives, and the base 208 capacity is left alone so the finale still requires the maxed shield.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The module's twelve committed-descent cells all report survives:false, but the sweep does not say which capacity it judged against. Against the 208 base it is right everywhere; against the 238 maxed tier the bottom (223.3) and top (231.3) skimmed cases are already under. Either the check uses base capacity or the finale is genuinely dead — I propose the shield raise on the assumption it is the former, and a human should confirm which before flying it.\",\n    \"The ascent failures at the middle and top samples were flown on the base ship. The GDD never claims the base ship reaches those altitudes, so 'crashed on ascent' at 115 km and 215 km is expected; what is not expected is a 1.4% margin at the bottom, and that is the number I acted on. The sweep does not fly upgraded ships, so nothing here measures whether tier-1 or tier-2 flight parts open the upper band.\",\n    \"The exploration grid's top-scoring worlds are all radius 800 m with a 224 m atmosphere — physically absurd toy planets that happen to satisfy seven targets. Read the satisfaction rates, not the top list: the rates are what say unstaged_pass_survivable (8.0%), fuel_margin_sane (16.4%), greed_costs_something (16.7%) and full_hold_lands_soft (22.2%) are design problems, and the specific worlds are not proposals.\",\n    \"Every touchdown speed in the sweep is a point mass under a perfect flare — 3.00 m/s empty and 3.27 m/s full hold at every altitude, with spread_across_bands_ms of exactly 0. Real deploy timing, attitude error and a player who panics will all push these up, so the 5.0 m/s soft line has less margin in play than the table shows, and the module's 7.69 m/s hard touchdown is a floor rather than a typical outcome.\",\n    \"The skim multipliers saturate to zero benefit after the first pass at every entry depth scanned, which is cleaner than any real atmosphere would give. If the simulator is modelling the skim as a single fixed-altitude bite rather than an integrated pass, the second and third skims would be under-credited — that is the one place I suspect the model rather than the numbers.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":41790,"ttft_stream_ms":2650,"time_to_request_ms":324,"type":"result","duration_ms":102544,"uuid":"89ff5dee-c783-4123-bf86-5e323f2054a8"}
